# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run output. None of it is an input to anything, and all of it is regenerated
# by re-running the config that produced it -- which IS tracked. A published
# repository carries what is needed to reproduce a result, not the transcript
# of every attempt (D38).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
data/
outputs/
logs/
manifests/
Report/
aux_py/

# docs/ and configs/ are TRACKED as of the simulation phase.
# docs/ carries docs_decisions.md, AUDIT_v*, BENDERS_SPEC_v* and the reference run
# logs those documents cite by name (e.g. baseline_d9_D30.log). configs/ carries the
# baseline fixtures every refactor is verified against. Without them a clone receives
# breaking changes -- notably a2d9e97, which voids every historical lower bound --
# with no record of why, and cannot reproduce the runs that justify them.

# Project-specific generated scenarios; keep only one example
setups/*
!setups/demo_cont_demand.yaml
# Run manifests (provenance for individual runs; regenerated per run)
manifests/

# Sweep and experiment scratch: scripts/sweep.py writes both of these, and the
# tables they produced are quoted in docs/ with their provenance.
configs/sweep/
configs/bench/

# configs/phase1/ is deliberately NOT ignored: those five configs reproduce the
# Phase 1 A/B table quoted in README.md, and a published repo carries what
# regenerates a result (D38).
#
# docs/phase1/ IS ignored. It is a working research document, not a finding. Its
# reading rules -- the conditions that stop the A/B table being misquoted -- are
# inlined into README.md, which is where they have to survive.
docs/phase1/
docs/sweep/
docs/AUDIT_v3.md
docs/BENDERS_SPEC_v3.md
docs/HANDLER_CENSUS.md
docs/SESSION_TOOLING.md
docs/design.md

handout.md

# The live experiment config. It is edited constantly -- by runs, by sweeps, and
# by the parallel external audit working in this same folder -- and none of those
# edits belong in a commit. configs/default.example.yaml is the tracked copy:
#
#     cp configs/default.example.yaml configs/default.yaml
#
configs/default.yaml